// =====================================================================
// RS_Main SNDINFO
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Layout follows the project asset directive (docs/DIRECTIVE_GNRC_REIMPORT.md
// section 1): a path answers "does one weapon own this, or is it shared?"
//
//   sounds/rs_weapon/vr_<weapon>/     main arsenal, one folder per weapon
//   sounds/rs_vp_weapon/vp_<weapon>/  Vanilla+ set, one folder per weapon
//   sounds/combatfx/<category>/       SHARED effects -- owned by no weapon
//        casings/ ricochet/ impact/ magdrops/ explosions/
//        foley/ melee/
//   sounds/hq_vanilla/                the HQ vanilla alternate pack
//
// A per-weapon folder holds ONLY that weapon's own fire/reload/handling
// audio. Anything both sets can consume -- casings, ricochets, impacts,
// magazine drops, explosions, foley -- lives under combatfx/ instead,
// mirroring the sprites/combatfx/ tree category-for-category: the same
// effect is found under the same category name on both sides, so
// "explosions" means sprites/combatfx/explosions AND
// sounds/combatfx/explosions. That one-name-two-places rule is what lets
// the affix system assemble an effect's visual and audio together,
// rather than hunting through whichever weapon folder an asset happened
// to land in first.
//
// sounds/UNUSED/ (pre-reorg originals) was emptied of everything that
// existed nowhere else -- SAWCORD to vp_chainsaw, the extra DSDBLOD
// takes to vp_supershotgun, melee/bat takes to combatfx/melee, alternate
// encodings back to their weapon folders -- and is now fully redundant.
//
// Every entry below is verified against what each weapon's own .zs code
// actually calls (A_PlaySound/A_StartSound), not against what a folder
// happens to contain.
//
// Paths use the lowercase folder names that actually exist on disk
// (vr_pistol, not VR_Pistol) -- avoids the exact case-sensitivity trap
// already found and fixed in the Revolver MODELDEF earlier in this
// project; a case mismatch here is silently fine on Windows but breaks
// on any case-sensitive packaging.
// =====================================================================

